summary:
V40 — Backend testing for Axon AI assistant SSE streaming + global semantic cache (Jaccard 0.75, TTL 7d). All 11 tests passed (100%). Verified: 1) POST /api/assistant/chat/stream returns Content-Type: text/event-stream with proper SSE format (event: <name>
data: <json>

), emitting exactly one meta, ≥2 delta chunks and exactly one done event; concatenated deltas produce a coherent Italian reply. 2) Cache HIT: identical query returns from_cache=true with cache_similarity=1.0 in ~0.3s (well under 2s target). 3) Semantic HIT: rephrased PUN query returns similarity=0.833 (>=0.75). 4) Cache BYPASS: CRM-bound query (miei/appuntamenti/oggi tokens) and short query (PUN, 3 chars) both correctly return from_cache=false. 5) Non-streaming POST /api/assistant/chat also honours cache (returned from_cache=true, similarity=1.0 for PUN rephrase). 6) Error handling: empty message and >4000 chars both return HTTPException 400 raised before StreamingResponse (direct HTTP 400 response); missing auth returns 401. 7) Persistence verified via GET /api/assistant/history — both user and assistant messages saved to db.assistant_messages after streaming call.
